eering, Case Western Reserve University, Cleveland, Ohio."}]}}, {"fullName": "Alilou M", "lastName": "Alilou", "firstName": "Mehdi", "initials": "M", "authorAffiliationDetailsList": {"authorAffiliation": [{"affiliation": "Department of Biomedical Engineering, Case Western Reserve University, Cleveland, Ohio."}]}}, {"fullName": "Bera K", "lastName": "Bera", "firstName": "Kaustav", "initials": "K", "authorId": {"type": "ORCID", "value": "0000-0001-9831-6000"}, "authorAffiliationDetailsList": {"authorAffiliation": [{"affiliation": "Department of Biomedical Engineering, Case Western Reserve University, Cleveland, Ohio."}]}}, {"fullName": "Fu P", "lastName": "Fu", "firstName": "Pingfu", "initials": "P", "authorId": {"type": "ORCID", "value": "0000-0002-2334-5218"}, "authorAffiliationDetailsList": {"authorAffiliation": [{"affiliation": "Department of Population and Quantitative Health Sciences, CWRU, Cleveland, Ohio."}]}}, {"fullName": "Feldman M", "lastName": "Feldman", "firstName": "Michael", "initials": "M", "authorId": {"type": "ORCID", "value": "0000-0002-6661-4940"}, "authorAffiliationDetailsList": {"authorAffiliation": [{"affiliation": "Pathology and Laboratory Medicine, Hospital of the University of Pennsylvania, Philadelphia, Pennsylvania."}]}}, {"fullName": "Velcheti V", "lastName": "Velcheti", "firstName": "Vamsidhar", "initials": "V", "authorAffiliationDetailsList": {"authorAffiliation": [{"affiliation": "Department of Hematology and Oncology, NYU Langone Health, New York, New York."}]}}, {"fullName": "Madabhushi A", "lastName": "Madabhushi", "firstName": "Anant", "initials": "A", "authorId": {"type": "ORCID", "value": "0000-0002-5741-0399"}, "authorAffiliationDetailsList": {"authorAffiliation": [{"affiliation": "Department of Biomedical Engineering, Case Western Reserve University, Cleveland, Ohio. axm788@case.edu."}, {"affiliation": "Louis Stokes Cleveland Veterans Administration Medical Center, Cleveland, Ohio."}]}}]}, "authorIdList": {"authorId": [{"type": "ORCID", "value": "0000-0001-5345-6763"}, {"type": "ORCID", "value": "0000-0001-9831-6000"}, {"type": "ORCID", "value": "0000-0002-2334-5218"}, {"type": "ORCID", "value": "0000-0002-3068-3573"}, {"type": "ORCID", "value": "0000-0002-4141-8548"}, {"type": "ORCID", "value": "0000-0002-5378-9434"}, {"type": "ORCID", "value": "0000-0002-5741-0399"}, {"type": "ORCID", "value": "0000-0002-6661-4940"}, {"type": "ORCID", "value": "0000-0003-3002-0937"}]}, "dataLinksTagsList": {"dataLinkstag": ["altmetrics", "supporting_data"]}, "journalInfo": {"issue": "1", "volume": "8", "journalIssueId": 2898627, "dateOfPublication": "2020 Jan", "monthOfPublication": 1, "yearOfPublication": 2020, "journal": {"medlineAbbreviation": "Cancer Immunol Res", "title": "Cancer immunology research", "essn": "2326-6074", "issn": "2326-6066", "nlmid": "101614637", "isoabbreviation": "Cancer Immunol Res"}, "printPublicationDate": "2020-01-01"}, "pubYear": "2020", "pageInfo": "108-119", "abstractText": "No predictive biomarkers can robustly identify patients with non-small cell lung cancer (NSCLC) who will benefit from immune checkpoint inhibitor (ICI) therapies. Here, in a machine learning setting, we compared changes (\"delta\") in the radiomic texture (DelRADx) of CT patterns both within and outside tumor nodules before and after two to three cycles of ICI therapy. We found that DelRADx patterns could predict response to ICI therapy and overall survival (OS) for patients with NSCLC. We retrospectively analyzed data acquired from 139 patients with NSCLC at two institutions, who were divided into a discovery set (D<sub>1</sub> = 50) and two independent validation sets (D<sub>2</sub> = 62, D<sub>3</sub> = 27). Intranodular and perinodular texture descriptors were extracted, and the relative differences were computed. A linear discriminant analysis (LDA) classifier was trained with 8 DelRADx features to predict RECIST-derived response. Association of delta-radiomic risk score (DRS) with OS was determined. The association of DelRADx features with tumor-infiltrating lymphocyte (TIL) density on the diagnostic biopsies (<i>n</i> = 36) was also evaluated. The LDA classifier yielded an AUC of 0.88 ± 0.08 in distinguishing responders from nonresponders in D<sub>1</sub>, and 0.85 and 0.81 in D<sub>2</sub> and D<sub>3</sub> DRS was associated with OS [HR: 1.64; 95% confidence interval (CI), 1.22-2.21; <i>P</i> = 0.0011; C-index = 0.72). Peritumoral Gabor features were associated with the density of TILs on diagnostic biopsy samples. Our results show that DelRADx could be used to identify early functional responses in patients with NSCLC.", "affiliation": "Department of Biomedical Engineering, Case Western Reserve University, Cleveland, Ohio.", "publicationStatus": "ppublish", "language": "eng", "pubModel": "Print-Electronic", "pubTypeList": {"pubType": ["Research Support, Non-U.S. Gov't", "research-article", "Research Support, U.S. Gov't, Non-P.H.S.", "Journal Article", "Research Support, N.I.H., Extramural"]}, "grantsList": {"grant": [{"agency": "National Center for Research Resources", "grantId": "1 C06 RR12463-01", "orderIn": 0}, {"agency": "NCI NIH", "grantId": "1U24CA199374-01", "orderIn": 0}, {"agency": "NCI NIH", "grantId": "R01CA202752-01A1", "orderIn": 0}, {"agency": "BLRD VA", "acronym": "BX", "grantId": "I01 BX004121", "orderIn": 0}, {"agency": "NCI NIH HHS", "acronym": "CA", "grantId": "R01 CA202752", "orderIn": 0}, {"agency": "NCI NIH HHS", "acronym": "CA", "grantId": "R01 CA208236", "orderIn": 0}, {"agency": "NCI NIH", "grantId": "R01CA216579-01A1", "orderIn": 0}, {"agency": "NCI NIH HHS", "acronym": "CA", "grantId": "U01 CA239055", "orderIn": 0}, {"agency": "NIBIB NIH HHS", "acronym": "EB", "grantId": "R43 EB028736", "orderIn": 0}, {"agency": "NCI NIH HHS", "acronym": "CA", "grantId": "U24 CA199374", "orderIn": 0}, {"agency": "NCI NIH HHS", "acronym": "CA", "grantId": "R01 CA216579", "orderIn": 0}, {"agency": "NCI NIH HHS", "acronym": "CA", "grantId": "R01